    intermediate: "The 'King Save': If you already have cards that fit on a King, wait for an opponent to play their King into a corner first so you don't have to waste your turn filling a corner slot.",
    advanced: 'Sequence Consolidation: Always look for ways to merge existing table piles. This frees up the 4 main slots, which can then be filled with any card, potentially dumping a large part of your hand at once.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't build too deep on the 4 main piles if you have a King; you want the Corners to be most accessible.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Watch your opponents' colors. If they are primarily drawing Red cards, try to play Black cards to the board to entice them to 'tack' their cards onto yours.",
